{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793009478,"nonce":"hKPKZjvb6v1KEk3jjhURFWSfARc=","title":"Synchronize durable cloud workspace state across desktop, browser and compute","message":"Parent plan: e003324b4983bd187aa32106d22f198e4ad218eebe4eea5edb10793ef31e4b1a\n\nMove authoritative acknowledged text updates/checkpoints and workspace generations behind the Durable Object/R2 authority, reusing Yjs/Yrs and stable document IDs across moves. Existing native compute-process authority is not sufficient for restart-safe Cloud Sync. Connect native desktop and browser edits to the same protocol; persist before durable acknowledgements and compact logs without retaining an entire large workspace in actor RAM. Serialize file-tree, binary and Git/index changes against base revisions; merge offline text where supported, preserve conflicting binary/Git versions and expose resolution. Materialize a fenced revision into the existing MSB provider seam, reconcile compute file watchers through the same authority, and use flush barriers before build/run or suspend. No second independent filesystem writer may overwrite CRDT state. Verify close-originating-desktop, browser edit, kill/recreate compute, restore and sync-back with no lost acknowledged edits.","files":null}]}